From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:00:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Mac font-aware canvas text measurements

Resolve the canvas font shorthand into a fixed Mac desktop font profile
and select the first available family. Handle quoted/multiword names,
case, CSS escapes, generic families, unknown fallbacks and line-height.
Reject malformed assignments without changing the current font state.

Use representative Helvetica/Times-Roman ASCII glyph advances and a
fixed-pitch model, retaining the Unicode combining/wide-glyph fallback.
Regular and offscreen canvases share the same native implementation and
TextMetrics bridge. Leave DOM/SVG measurement and canvas rasterisation
unchanged. Update only existing upstream numeric assertions; add no tests.

This is a deterministic MacBook Neo measurement mock: families alias
three representative faces, vertical bounds remain synthetic, and no
kerning, style-specific shaping or exact CoreText fidelity is claimed.
No macOS-version-specific font/metric claim is made.

Metric sources and retained Adobe permission/copyright:
https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib/tree/v3.10.7/lib/matplotlib/mpl-data/fonts/pdfcorefonts
Extract only ASCII WX values from Helvetica.afm and Times-Roman.afm.
Supplemental desktop Chrome parsing checks verify zero sizes, unknown
fallbacks, quoted/escaped families, invalid assignments and line-height;
these are not claimed as a macOS metric calibration.

Temporary diagnostics validate 31 checks plus native shape/receiver,
regular/offscreen/iframe parity, isolation, retained metrics and
navigation reset. Reviewer-discovered opposite-quote handling is fixed.
Full upstream tests pass (1658/1658). Benchmark validation is recorded in
ignored .build artifacts after export; no benchmark predicates change.
